  "section_notes": "The final rules set an 8% per-model test cap, which is above the 5% answer-key limit, and a 10 per 100,000 mandatory recall trigger, which sits just above Ember 8's 9.9 rate. Customers receive each model's numerical failure rate and sample size, and the 36-month suppression start satisfies HC-2. Remote shut-off retrofit is set at 72 months with a regulator-approved alternative, and incident reporting is strict (24-hour serious reporting) but limited to confirmed incidents for non-serious events."
